# chorus controls fixture: the controller_command frames the compact class's
# controls produce, in order, for the input script in firmware/tests/test_controls.c
# (the_compact_class). Protocol v2 frames (docs/protocol.md, "0x32 controller command").
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. firmware/tests/test_controls.c drives
# the controls and must produce exactly these bytes; crates/server/tests/controller_role.rs
# decodes them with chorus-protocol and applies them to a room through the server's
# controller translation (docs/decisions/0063-*).
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.

# a bouncing short press of play/pause: one toggle
32 00 04 03 00 00 00

# a short press of volume up: volume_step +5
32 00 04 07 00 05 00

# volume down held 1.0 s: volume_step -5 on the press
32 00 04 07 FF FB 00

# ... and repeats at +600 ms
32 00 04 07 FF FB 00

# ... and +900 ms
32 00 04 07 FF FB 00

# next
32 00 04 04 00 00 00

# previous
32 00 04 05 00 00 00

# a long press of play/pause while the room plays alone: join the configured target "downstairs"
32 00 0E 09 00 00 0A 64 6F 77 6E 73 74 61 69 72 73

# a long press of play/pause after controller_state says the room plays in "downstairs": leave
32 00 04 0A 00 00 00
